# SABOTAGE: CF-17(c) (ADR-048 §6) — `context_gate/6`'s SECOND CONJUNCT IS DROPPED. The
# `foldable(views, lines) == []` half of the LEVEL 1 / LEVEL 3 boundary is removed, so the
# gate ends a run the instant its assembled context crosses `max_input_tokens` — without
# ever asking whether a span is still eligible to fold. §6 defines Level 3 as "a context
# that does not fit under it with NOTHING eligible left to fold"; this build fires on the
# first half of that sentence alone, and a run that a later turn's Level 1 fold would have
# rescued takes the `:context_exhausted` terminal instead.
#
# This is the coverage gap CF-17(c) named: before `test/ai/agent_context_gate_test.exs`
# shipped, `grep -rn context_gate samen_core/test` returned ZERO hits and this deletion
# passed the whole suite. The comment shipped directly above the gate CLAIMS "this gate
# cannot be satisfied by a constant" — that claim is what this patch, and the test it
# flips, turn into a measurement.
#
# Flips the RESCUED arm ONLY. Everything else stays GREEN, which is what makes the red mean
# what it says: the EXHAUSTED CONTROL in the same file (same ceiling, same script shape,
# the bulk text simply on turn one instead of turn two, so NOTHING is eligible to fold)
# still passes — both before and after — so the red fails because the foldable conjunct is
# gone, not because the gate, the ceiling, or the Level 3 terminal broke. `P3`'s two arms
# in `agent_compaction_test.exs` are likewise untouched: they exercise the FIRST conjunct,
# which this patch leaves intact.
#
# `views` is renamed to `_views` in the head in the same hunk — not extra scope, it is what
# "the conjunct is gone" means here: the parameter has no remaining reader and leaving it
# named would trip Elixir's unused-variable warning under `--warnings-as-errors`, so the
# patch would fail to COMPILE instead of failing the named test. `foldable/2` itself keeps
# its other caller (`fold_span/6`) and is untouched. Touches agent.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_context_gate_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: CF-17(c) RESCUED: a run OVER max_input_tokens that STILL HAS a foldable span does NOT end :context_exhausted
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
@@ -1263,9 +1263,14 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Agent do
   #
   # Under the ceiling the turn proceeds unchanged, which is what every shipped agent test
   # exercises — so this gate cannot be satisfied by a constant.
-  defp context_gate(%Run{} = run, views, definition, tools, goal, lines) do
-    if context_tokens(definition, tools, goal, lines) > run.max_input_tokens and
-         foldable(views, lines) == [] do
+  defp context_gate(%Run{} = run, _views, definition, tools, goal, lines) do
+    # SABOTAGE (CF-17(c), ADR-048 §6): the SECOND CONJUNCT is dropped. The gate now ends
+    # a run the moment its assembled context crosses `max_input_tokens`, WITHOUT asking
+    # whether anything is still eligible to fold — so a run a later turn's Level 1 fold
+    # would have rescued takes the Level 3 terminal instead. §6 defines Level 3 as "a
+    # context that does not fit under it with NOTHING eligible left to fold"; this is the
+    # gate firing on the first half of that sentence alone.
+    if context_tokens(definition, tools, goal, lines) > run.max_input_tokens do
       {:error, :context_exhausted}
     else
       :ok
